--     bundled instance `IntCommRing : CommRing Int int_add int_mul
--     int_zero int_one` — the first concrete instance, after which
--     `by ring with IntCommRing` works and `Int` becomes a self-module
--     (`smul := int_mul`) reusing the distributivity laws.
--   * Ideal predicates, quotient rings R/I, localization S⁻¹R — need
--     relation-parameterized HIT quotients (research-level under the
--     current HIT support).
--   * Polynomial rings R[X] (list encoding) + evaluation homomorphism.
--   * Finite fields F_p = Z/p.
